% Prolog compatibility shim. In Prolog, `library(chr)` is the runtime
% that CHR programs are written against. In YCHR, CHR is the language
% itself -- `chr_constraint`, `chr_type` and the rule syntax are built
% in -- so this module is deliberately empty and exports nothing.
%
% It exists so that a Prolog module whose only YCHR-incompatible line is
% `:- use_module(library(chr)).` compiles unchanged, as long as the rest
% of the module is Prolog-compatible.

:- module(chr, []).
